<title>BRAZIL: Brazil likely to see gradual rise in orange output.</title>
<headline>Brazil likely to see gradual rise in orange output.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian orange production is likely to grow slowly over the next five years and will depend on weather conditions and farmer returns, said the head of the Brazilian Citrus Exporters' Association (Abecitrus).</p>
<p>&quot;The chances are we will see gradually increasing production over the next five years, with possible strong variations depending on climate conditions and return for the grower,&quot; Ademerval Garcia said in a speech made available to Reuters.</p>
</text>
